KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ plain value-pack decltype resolves: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
A variadic function template whose trailing-return decltype contains a plain
by-value value-pack expansion f(a...) -- with no type parameter pack reference
in the pattern -- is not expanded, so decltype(invk(...)) silently fails
vacuously.  The forwarding-cast form static_cast<Args&&>(a)... is handled
because it references the type pack Args.  Flip to CORE once a bare value
parameter pack is expanded in a trailing-return decltype.
